1. Project Overview 
1.1 Purpose 
The purpose of this system is to create a centralized Laravel-based Order 
Management System (OMS) that integrates with the Shopify store to automate order 
assignment, track order progress, and measure staff performance. 
The OMS will: 
 Fetch new orders from Shopify via API. 
 Distribute orders equally among staff automatically every 15 minutes. 
 Allow each staff member to manage the full lifecycle of assigned orders — from 
confirmation to delivery. 
 Synchronize order statuses and tags with Shopify in real time. 
 Generate detailed performance and activity reports for management. 
2. Scope of the System 
2.1 System Objectives 
 Automate order fetching and staff assignment. 
 Provide complete order tracking and workflow visibility. 
 Maintain synchronization between Shopify and Laravel OMS. 
 Provide real-time status updates and tagging in Shopify. 
 Generate performance analytics and reporting for each staff member. 
2.2 Expected Users 
 Admin: Has full control over system, users, and reports. 
 Staff: Handles assigned orders (confirmation, packaging, delivery, etc.). 
 System (Cron): Automatically fetches and assigns orders. 
3. Functional Requirements 
3.1 Integration with Shopify 
 Connect via Shopify REST API or GraphQL API. 
 Fetch new orders periodically (every 15 minutes). 
 Update order tags and statuses on Shopify whenever changes occur in OMS. 
 Sync order details including: 
o Order ID 
o Customer name & contact 
o Order items 
o Quantity, price, payment method 
o Shipping address 
o Current status 
o Shopify tags 
3.2 Order Assignment Module 
 Cron job will run every 15 minutes. 
 New unassigned orders will be equally distributed among all active staff. 
 If there are unprocessed orders from previous batch, they should not be 
reassigned. 
 Each assigned order will be linked to: 
o Assigned staff member 
o Assigned timestamp 
o Order source (Shopify) 
 Admin can manually reassign orders if needed. 
3.3 Order Workflow Management 
Each staff member will have access to assigned orders with the following workflow: 
